meta {
  name: Update Tenant Branding - fine-tuned colour roles
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

put {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/tenant/branding
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Cookie: auth_token={{authToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "seed_hex": "#0d4668",
    "color_overrides": {
      "light": { "primary": "#0a3a58", "secondary": "#4a5568" },
      "dark": { "primary": "#9dccf4" }
    }
  }
}

docs {
  admin.branding.manage, theme unlocked. color_overrides is SPARSE: only the roles that were
  changed, per mode (light / dark); every other role keeps following the seed. Send {} to clear all.

  Editable roles (23): primary, onPrimary, primaryContainer, onPrimaryContainer, secondary,
  onSecondary, secondaryContainer, onSecondaryContainer, tertiary, onTertiary, tertiaryContainer,
  onTertiaryContainer, background, surface, surfaceContainerLowest, surfaceContainerLow,
  surfaceContainer, surfaceContainerHigh, surfaceContainerHighest, onSurface, onSurfaceVariant,
  outline, outlineVariant. Values are #rrggbb.

  422 when a role is not in that list (error and status colours are fixed), a value is not #rrggbb,
  or a mode other than light/dark is sent.
  422 COLOR_CONTRAST (details.pairs lists them) when text would fall under 3:1 against its
  background once the shades are applied over the ones the seed derives - checked against the seed
  that will be in force, so a seed change alone can trip it.
  403 BRANDING_THEME_LOCKED while Super Admin has locked the theme (the database trigger enforces it too).

  A user's own override uses PUT /me/preferences/theme with the same color_overrides shape; it is
  only honoured while the tenant theme is unlocked.
}
